From 9b6f2915bfa276b01b763a908ffa2a3f9b82f765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:42:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] l2r-local: entry 19: retcon destructors' direct arms in
 one function per type (reussir#759 option a+)

A drop of a variant whose destructor is retcon (RecordDropKind::Worklist)
and that has a direct arm was expanded in place at every drop site: each
direct arm's member drops inline, and through them the same expansion of
every nested type of the same kind, with no outlining and no size limit.
One site held the whole unfolded tree of direct-arm drops, so code size was
exponential in type nesting (5 nested types: rrc above 12 GiB; lean2rr's
closure enums with 150+ arms: above 10 GiB) and quadratic in the number of
arms of one type (reussir-lang/reussir#759, option (a+) there, which the
maintainer chose; kept as a local patch).

The direct-arm path is now emitted once per type, as `<dtor>.direct`: a
plain (non-coroutine) linkonce_odr function that dispatches on the tag,
drops a direct arm in place (one level: a nested type's drop is a call to
its own `.direct` or destructor) and calls the retcon destructor for every
other arm.

- A drop site outside a retcon destructor calls `<dtor>.direct`.
- A drop site inside a retcon destructor tests the tag once against a
  constant mask, `(MASK >> tag) & 1`: a set bit calls `<dtor>.direct`, a
  clear bit suspends into the running executor (`reussir.dtor.suspend`),
  as before. MASK has the direct arms whose drop cannot run a retcon
  destructor (cannot reach a Worklist record; a memoized walk over the
  member types). A direct arm that holds a retcon value suspends too, so
  that value is dropped in the running executor instead of starting its
  own. The site is O(1) in the number of arms: a `record.dispatch` there
  lowered to one block per tag, which CoroSplit then copied into every
  resume clone.

Upstream #800's load forwarding runs after the expansion as before, on
every function including the `.direct` ones.

Tests: conversion/retcon_drop_leaf.mlir checks the new shapes (the
`.direct` function, the root site's call, the masked test inside a retcon
destructor); conversion/retcon_drop_direct_nested.mlir checks that a
nested retcon type's drop inside `.direct` is a call to that type's
`.direct` (no copy of its arms) and that a direct arm holding a retcon
value is left out of the mask.
